 be less harmful  as it contains citrate and lactate which  are produced due to the fermentation  process  these along with the calcium present in  the curd help to neutralize the highly  acidic  hydrochloric acid or hcl that our  stomach produces  a study even showed that curd may cure  the infection caused by the bacteria h  pylori  which is the most common cause of  acidity due to stomach infections  also curd is a probiotic rich food which  helps the good bacteria in our gut to  grow properly  that are very important for healthy  digestion the best way to have curd is  to have it first thing on an empty  stomach  diluted with water you can eat it with  fruits  or even make curd rice start to include  curd in your daily diet it will  definitely make a difference in the  symptoms of facility  i hope i was able to answer the question  if you liked the video  make sure to share this video with your  family friends and any person you know  who might be suffering from acid reflux  you can support med simplified by  joining our channel here on youtube or  becoming a member at our patreon page  links are in the description below thank  you so much for watching and see you in  the next video
 

